Walking.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:16.290
Hi!

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.000
Unfamiliar ceiling.

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:16.280
So the angels have returned it's rather sudden it's the same as it was 15 years ago

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:22.880
That's the way of disasters they come without warning on the positive side our previous

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:30.000
Investments would appear to be not such a waste after all you can't be sure about that yet if it doesn't pay off

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.000
It's still a waste.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.000
Correct.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:36.000
Now that news of the Angels has become common knowledge,

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:43.070
Nerve must take steps to control the manner in which this information is received by the general public.

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:47.730
You may rest assured that it's already been taken care of.

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:48.680
Don't worry.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:55.980
Government officials have announced that in regard to the declaration of this incident...

00:04:55.980 --> 00:05:00.000
Ah, public scenario B-22. Just like we thought.

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:02.760
- So we're covering up the truth again?

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:05.060
- Well, at least the PR people are happy.

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:07.160
They've finally got something to do.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:09.900
- We're being pretty casual about it.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:11.200
- I don't think so.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.620
Actually, I think we're all pretty scared.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.580
- Of course we are.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:17.820
- Well, we must acknowledge that.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:21.340
- But still, I wonder, Mr. Ikari,

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:23.690
were Nerve and Ava used efficiently?

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:25.610
- Repair costs for Unit One

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:29.130
added to the development costs for Unit Zero

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:30.000
are simply stupid.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:35.720
Staggering we also understand that you gave that toy to your own son time

00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:38.340
money and manpower

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:43.510
How much more will be wasted by you and your family and that is not your only?

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:48.130
Responsibility the human enhancement project that should be your top priority

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:55.420
Correct under these desperate circumstances that project may be the only real hope for the future of mankind

00:05:55.940 --> 00:06:00.000
Do you understand in any event the angels are no excuse?

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:03.910
excuse for the delay in the schedule of that project.

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:06.150
We may consider adjusting the budget.

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:08.350
- The rest of the meeting does not concern you.

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:11.870
- Your presence here was appreciated.

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:19.860
- Ikari, you do know that there can be no turning back.

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:24.870
- I know, mankind has no time left.

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:54.430
Air conditioning's the greatest thing.

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:56.300
Men's triumph over nature.

00:06:57.220 --> 00:06:58.740
Shinji's finally woken up.

00:06:59.360 --> 00:06:59.860
And...

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:02.790
- How is he?

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:05.430
- Well, his memory seems a bit muddled, but--

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:08.200
- You don't think it could be contamination, do you?

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:10.400
- I don't think we should worry.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:12.840
- Really?

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:13.740
You're right.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:16.060
He did have a pretty hectic day.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:17.220
- Poor little kid.

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:20.200
His cerebellum must have taken a lot of stress.

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:21.380
- Cerebellum?

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:22.620
Don't you mean his heart?

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:53.060
- If Ava and this city both operated their full potential,

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:54.970
we might make it through this.

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:56.910
- You're such an optimist.

00:07:56.910 --> 00:08:00.000
- Hey, sometimes you need a little wishful thinking

00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:06.480
fun living. I see your point. It's nice to hear a positive attitude. I'll see you later.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:15.210
Okay. See ya. Dr. Ugai, internal department one. Dr. Ugai, internal department one. Please call

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:20.960
Dr. Azuma of the first surgical department immediately. The medical conference regarding

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:26.740
the B experiment will be held as scheduled. All supervisors, please proceed to conference room two.

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:50.500
- They don't wanna live together?

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:51.950
Are you sure?

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:55.530
- I think that living apart is natural to them.

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:58.070
- And being together is unnatural?

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:02.970
He'll be living alone?

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:07.400
That's right. His room will be on the 6th block beyond this one. Is that alright?

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:08.740
Yes, sir.

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:12.710
Shinji? Are you sure about that?

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:17.320
Living alone... is fine with me. I'm alone anyway.

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:19.550
WHAT DID YOU SAY?!

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:24.220
You heard me! I said I'll be taking Shinji home to live in my place, okay?

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:30.000
It's already been approved. And don't worry, I'm not gonna be making any passes at him.

00:09:33.930 --> 00:09:42.490
- Some people don't have any sense of humor.

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:44.540
Party tonight, huh?

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:45.600
- Why is that?

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:47.060
- It's a welcoming party in honor

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:49.110
of my new roommate, of course.

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:07.600
Yes, I'd never have dreamt that this city would become a battlefield.

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:08.600
Yeah.

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:11.520
My husband's saying that at least the kids and I should move.

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:12.520
Don't I know it.

00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:15.520
This city may be a fortress, but that's no guarantee of safety.

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:23.150
Just thinking about last night...

00:10:23.150 --> 00:10:25.150
I hope you don't mind if we make a little stop on the way.

00:10:25.150 --> 00:10:26.430
A stop where?

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:29.320
Oh, it's a really cool place.

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:41.020
- It's so desolate, the city seems so lonely.

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:41.970
- Here we go.

00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:26.160
- It's awesome, things are growing.

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:27.810
- Designed to stand against the angels.

00:11:30.380 --> 00:11:36.400
Tokyo 3. This is our city, and it's the city that you saved.

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:59.000
To have been delivered already, Shinji. I just moved here myself, you know?

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:02.960
Hey, come in.

00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:06.970
Uh, I don't want to intrude.

00:12:07.720 --> 00:12:10.390
Shinji, this is your home now.

00:12:15.260 --> 00:12:20.140
I'm, I'm home.

00:12:20.790 --> 00:12:21.890
Welcome home.

00:12:22.210 --> 00:12:30.000
As you can see, the place is just a little bit messy, but, uh, go ahead and make yourself comfortable.

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:32.950
This is... a little messy?

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:37.990
Could you put the food in the fridge, please?

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:39.490
Uh, yes, ma'am.

00:12:40.330 --> 00:12:40.890
Ice?

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:42.520
Snack?

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:46.450
Gallons of beer?

00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:49.060
What kind of life does she lead?

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:50.770
Huh.

00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:57.260
Uh, excuse me.

00:12:57.500 --> 00:12:58.930
What's in the other fridge?

00:12:59.050 --> 00:13:00.000
Oh, don't mind that.

00:13:03.390 --> 00:13:06.010
- Sleeping?

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:07.580
- Let's eat.

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:09.410
- Yeah, let's eat.

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:23.030
- You know, life just doesn't get any better than this.

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:24.160
Hmm?

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:25.140
Not hungry?

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:28.510
It's good, even if it is all instant.

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:29.700
- I'm sorry.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.560
and just not use the food like this.

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:33.750
- What?

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.420
- Arky.

00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:36.120
- Huh?

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:39.790
- No, that's not what, oh.

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:42.160
- Oh, isn't this nice?

00:13:42.160 --> 00:13:43.000
- Uh-huh.

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:45.600
- Having two for dinner sure beats eating alone, huh?

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:48.350
- Uh-huh.

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:49.500
- Here we go.

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:52.180
Let's go for the next one.

00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:55.550
Paper, scissors, stone.

00:13:55.550 --> 00:13:58.770
Three, two, one, go.

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:00.000
- Oh.

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:02.760
- Sorry, Shinji.

00:14:02.760 --> 00:14:04.790
Okay, that was a really fair way

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:07.780
to split up the chores, wasn't it?

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:08.800
- Yeah.

00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:09.720
- This is your home,

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:12.520
so feel free to take advantage of everything here.

00:14:12.520 --> 00:14:15.180
Except, of course, of me, that is.

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:17.330
- Uh, yes, ma'am.

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:18.670
- Yes, yes, yes.

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:20.210
Is that all you can say?

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:22.170
- It's getting on my nerves!

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:23.970
You're a boy, act like one!

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:25.050
- Yes, ma'am!

00:14:26.070 --> 00:14:28.090
- I guess that's just the way you are.

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:30.000
Why don't you go take a bath?

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:55.060
your troubles bathing cleans the mind and soul oh water penguins

00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:05.830
That was- that was a wha- what?

00:15:05.830 --> 00:15:09.460
His name's Pen Pen. He's your other roommate.

00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:12.890
Why don't you cover up?

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:14.400
Uh-huh.

00:15:14.400 --> 00:15:17.180
Oh!

00:15:17.180 --> 00:15:21.410
I should be nicer, but...

00:15:21.410 --> 00:15:24.160
He probably already made up his mind about me.

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:28.080
Misato...

00:15:28.080 --> 00:15:29.110
Kasaragi.

00:15:30.190 --> 00:15:31.490
She's not a bad person.

00:15:31.670 --> 00:15:33.430
Bathing clean to the mind and soul.

00:15:34.110 --> 00:15:36.830
But bad memories always seem to find me in the path.

00:15:38.060 --> 00:15:39.900
Like my father.

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:42.770
And that girl of Rey.

00:15:45.010 --> 00:15:48.030
So how was Rey today?

00:15:50.860 --> 00:15:53.320
You did see her at the hospital today, didn't you?

00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:56.920
She can work again in 20 days.

00:15:57.840 --> 00:16:00.000
By then, we'll be ready to reactivate Unit Zero

00:16:00.030 --> 00:16:05.830
from cryostasis it's so hard on these children there is no one else who can

00:16:05.830 --> 00:16:12.560
pilot the avas as long as they survive that is what I'll have them do with no

00:16:12.560 --> 00:16:14.180
regard to what they may want

00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:38.170
After all the horrible stuff he went through, I don't think he'll pilot again.

00:16:39.080 --> 00:16:40.600
Part of your job!

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:44.530
I'm just scared. I don't know how to deal with him.

00:16:44.960 --> 00:16:48.700
Grumbling already? But it was your idea to take him in, you know.

00:16:51.600 --> 00:16:58.000
I was just thinking of Shinji as a tool. I'm as shameless as Ritsuko.

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:03.790
We destroyed the angel, but I don't feel happy.

00:17:07.630 --> 00:17:09.190
Another unfamiliar ceiling.

00:17:11.680 --> 00:17:16.440
Of course, in this whole city, there's no place that's familiar.

00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:18.900
This is your home now.

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:21.530
Why am I here?

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:58.800
What about Shinji?

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:00.000
His monitors aren't reactive.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:01.500
His condition's unknown!

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:03.000
Unit 1's gone completely silent!

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:04.000
Misato!

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:05.370
We've got no choice!

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:06.870
Abort the operation!

00:18:06.870 --> 00:18:08.370
We've got to rescue the pilot!

00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:09.870
Eject the entry plug!

00:18:09.870 --> 00:18:10.870
We can't!

00:18:10.870 --> 00:18:12.370
It's completely out of control!

00:18:12.370 --> 00:18:13.370
What did you say?!

00:18:17.850 --> 00:18:23.250
Activating!

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:24.250
I don't believe it!

00:18:24.250 --> 00:18:25.160
This can't!

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:27.670
My god!

00:18:27.670 --> 00:18:29.350
Berserker!

00:19:07.100 --> 00:19:08.070
No way!

00:19:08.070 --> 00:19:16.480
It's neutralizing the base base!

00:19:16.480 --> 00:19:18.010
No!

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:23.340
It's breaking through it!

00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:25.700
It went through the 18th field like it wasn't there!

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:38.840
must be Ava's true form.

00:21:04.410 --> 00:21:04.930
Huh?

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:39.970
Shinji, can I come in?

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:45.240
I forgot to tell you something.

00:21:46.840 --> 00:21:49.800
You did something very good and very noble today.

00:21:50.590 --> 00:21:51.830
You should be proud.

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:53.810
Good night, Shinji.

00:21:56.790 --> 00:21:57.290
Hang in there.

00:22:01.560 --> 00:22:03.300
Fly to the

00:23:07.640 --> 00:23:12.340
Kenji's life is busier than ever, but he keeps to himself friendless until it's revealed that he's an Ava pilot.

00:23:12.660 --> 00:23:16.660
However, this new hero status brings both embarrassment and the rap of one boy in particular.

00:23:17.100 --> 00:23:20.040
Don't miss the next episode, and I'll sneak in a little bonus, okay?
